{"content_hash": "24018d98b960c88c", "version_id": 376, "article_id": 38, "level_code": "ja_n5", "lang": "ja", "level": 1, "level_label": "N5 初級", "title": "モナコの事件の男が話す", "title_zh": "摩纳哥爆炸案嫌疑人开口了", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckgel9044vqeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1661507916130-a957bb08d738?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8NXx8c3VzcGVjdCUyMGxpbmtlZCUyMG1vbmFjb3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTUzMzQ5fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Annie Spratt on Unsplash", "author": "Annie Spratt", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@anniespratt?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-view-of-a-city-GQ-ToCt9bm8?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(250, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(288, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "94a235c5d07a"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 363, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "モナコで6月、大きな事件がありました。お金持ちの男がけがをしました。ウクライナの男が今、話しました。", "lead_zh": "今年6月，摩纳哥发生了一起大案，一位富商受了伤。现在，一名乌克兰男子开口说话了。", "preview": "モナコで6月、ばくはつの事件がありました。ウクライナの男がけがをしました。男の子もけがをしました。とても大変でした。", "preview_zh": "今年6月，摩纳哥发生了一起爆炸事件。一名乌克兰男子受伤，他的儿子也受了伤，情况非常严重。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 366, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/38/ja_n5.mp3", "duration": 84.537, "size_bytes": 510912, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 272, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e8acbf2/content/data/versions/376.json", "paragraphs": ["モナコで6月、ばくはつの事件がありました。ウクライナの男がけがをしました。男の子もけがをしました。とても大変でした。", "ウクライナの元かんり官の男が、BBCに話しました。男は「ウクライナのHURが命令した」と言いました。HURはウクライナの軍のちょうさのきかんです。", "女の人がばくはつをおきました。女の人はカメラにうつっていました。女の人はそのあと、ウクライナのもりでしにました。あたまにたまが当たりました。", "男は「わたしはころしていない」と言います。男は「れいの男がやった」と言います。れいの男はHURの男です。れいの男ははじめ「わたしがやった」と言いました。でも、あとで「ちがう」と言いました。", "男は「この作戦はHURの上で決めた」と言います。男は「ばくはつのお金は5万ドル」と言います。女の人はお金をもらいに行きました。でも、もりでしにました。", "この事件はまだわかりません。ウクライナとモナコがしらべています。みんな「なぜ?」と思っています。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["今年6月，摩纳哥发生了一起爆炸事件。一名乌克兰男子受伤，他的儿子也受了伤，情况非常严重。", "一名乌克兰前安全官员向BBC讲述了情况。他说：“是乌克兰的HUR下的命令。”HUR是乌克兰军方的情报机构。", "一名女子安放了炸弹。她被监控摄像头拍到了。之后，她死在乌克兰的森林里，头部中枪。", "这名男子说：“我没有杀她。”他说：“是另一个男人干的。”那个男人是HUR的人。那个男人起初说“是我干的”，但后来又改口说“不是”。", "这名男子说：“这次行动是HUR高层决定的。”他还说：“爆炸的报酬是5万美元。”那名女子去拿钱，却死在了森林里。", "这起事件至今仍不清楚。乌克兰和摩纳哥正在调查。大家都在问：“为什么？”"], "body": "モナコで6月、ばくはつの事件がありました。ウクライナの男がけがをしました。男の子もけがをしました。とても大変でした。\n\nウクライナの元かんり官の男が、BBCに話しました。男は「ウクライナのHURが命令した」と言いました。HURはウクライナの軍のちょうさのきかんです。\n\n女の人がばくはつをおきました。女の人はカメラにうつっていました。女の人はそのあと、ウクライナのもりでしにました。あたまにたまが当たりました。\n\n男は「わたしはころしていない」と言います。男は「れいの男がやった」と言います。れいの男はHURの男です。れいの男ははじめ「わたしがやった」と言いました。でも、あとで「ちがう」と言いました。\n\n男は「この作戦はHURの上で決めた」と言います。男は「ばくはつのお金は5万ドル」と言います。女の人はお金をもらいに行きました。でも、もりでしにました。\n\nこの事件はまだわかりません。ウクライナとモナコがしらべています。みんな「なぜ?」と思っています。", "body_zh": "今年6月，摩纳哥发生了一起爆炸事件。一名乌克兰男子受伤，他的儿子也受了伤，情况非常严重。\n\n一名乌克兰前安全官员向BBC讲述了情况。他说：“是乌克兰的HUR下的命令。”HUR是乌克兰军方的情报机构。\n\n一名女子安放了炸弹。她被监控摄像头拍到了。之后，她死在乌克兰的森林里，头部中枪。\n\n这名男子说：“我没有杀她。”他说：“是另一个男人干的。”那个男人是HUR的人。那个男人起初说“是我干的”，但后来又改口说“不是”。\n\n这名男子说：“这次行动是HUR高层决定的。”他还说：“爆炸的报酬是5万美元。”那名女子去拿钱，却死在了森林里。\n\n这起事件至今仍不清楚。乌克兰和摩纳哥正在调查。大家都在问：“为什么？”", "text": "モナコで6月、ばくはつの事件がありました。ウクライナの男がけがをしました。男の子もけがをしました。とても大変でした。 ウクライナの元かんり官の男が、BBCに話しました。男は「ウクライナのHURが命令した」と言いました。HURはウクライナの軍のちょうさのきかんです。 女の人がばくはつをおきました。女の人はカメラにうつっていました。女の人はそのあと、ウクライナのもりでしにました。あたまにたまが当たりました。 男は「わたしはころしていない」と言います。男は「れいの男がやった」と言います。れいの男はHURの男です。れいの男ははじめ「わたしがやった」と言いました。でも、あとで「ちがう」と言いました。 男は「この作戦はHURの上で決めた」と言います。男は「ばくはつのお金は5万ドル」と言います。女の人はお金をもらいに行きました。でも、もりでしにました。 この事件はまだわかりません。ウクライナとモナコがしらべています。みんな「なぜ?」と思っています。", "vocab": [{"word": "事件", "pos": "noun", "zh": "事件", "note": "常见名词，指发生的事情"}, {"word": "けが", "pos": "noun", "zh": "受伤", "note": "受伤的意思"}, {"word": "話す", "pos": "verb", "zh": "说，讲", "note": "五段动词"}, {"word": "命令", "pos": "noun", "zh": "命令", "note": "上级下的指示"}, {"word": "女の人", "pos": "noun", "zh": "女人", "note": "指女性"}, {"word": "死ぬ", "pos": "verb", "zh": "死", "note": "五段动词"}, {"word": "お金", "pos": "noun", "zh": "钱", "note": "金钱"}, {"word": "わかる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "明白，清楚", "note": "五段动词"}], "title_original": "Suspect linked to Monaco bomb attack on millionaire breaks silence to BBC", "summary_original": "Vitalii Zhykovych gives his own account of the attempted assassination of Ukrainian-born businessman Vadym Yermolayev.", "body_original": "Suspect linked to Monaco bomb attack on millionaire breaks silence to BBC\nBy\nSarah Rainsford\n,\nSouthern and Eastern Europe correspondent\nand\nMariana Matveichuk\nPublished\n2 hours ago\nA former Ukrainian security services officer linked to a bomb attack in Monaco in June that targeted a multi-millionaire says he believed it was ordered by senior members of HUR, Ukraine's military intelligence agency.\nIn an exclusive interview with the BBC from prison in Kyiv, facilitated by his lawyer, Vitalii Zhykovych has given his own account of the attempted assassination for the first time.\nUkrainian-born businessman Vadym Yermolayev and his 13-year-old son were badly hurt in the blast and his partner suffered catastrophic injuries. Yermolayev later described their survival as \"nothing short of a miracle\".\nZhykovych describes himself as a \"freelancer\" for Ukraine's SBU security service and says Anastasia Berezovska, the woman caught on camera planting the bomb in Monaco, was his \"agent\".\nA week after the bombing, Berezovska's body was discovered in the woods west of Kyiv with gunshot wounds to the head.\nBut Zhykovych insists he did not send her to kill, and nor did he kill her.\nHe was arrested and accused of her murder together with an active-duty intelligence officer from HUR called Vladyslav Reut.\nReut initially confessed to investigators, and led them to the shallow grave. But days later in court, he changed his testimony to blame Zhykovych.\nUkrainian agent accused of murdering Monaco bomb suspect changes story\nPublished\n9 July\nFor a long time, Zhykovych himself stayed silent.\nNow, responding to questions from the BBC, he alleges that Reut - who he refers to as \"The Boss\" - had \"proposed the operation\" in Monaco against Vadym Yermolayev.\nHe understood it was an official mission.\n\"As Reut informed me, this operation […] had been authorised and approved by Reut's superiors, who served in the Main Intelligence Directorate of the Ministry of Defence [HUR],\" he says.\nDistancing himself from the explosion itself, he alleges that Reut asked to use Berezovska for the bombing and when Zhykovych refused – he says she was not fully trained – Reut agreed to send her for reconnaissance instead.\nReut then communicated directly with Bereszovska without including him, according to Zhykovych, who alleges that Reut also provided her with the explosives.\nThe BBC asked HUR to comment on the latest claims. The agency has previously said that it is \"committed to a full investigation\" and providing \"comprehensive support\" to law enforcement bodies.\nThe SBU has described Zhykovych in a statement only as a \"former law enforcement officer\".\nYermolayev was attacked in Monaco as he and his family were returning from an evening meal on the seafront. A surveillance video shows Berezovska walking slightly in front of the group, then leaving the device in a bag on their doorstep.\nIt detonates just as they get close, apparently shocking even Berezovska with its force.\nYermolayev later said he believed that serving HUR officers, \"individuals close to the agency's current and former leadership\", were linked to the attack.\nHe called for \"the truth, protection, and justice\".\nBerezovska was quickly identified as the suspected bomber and on 2 July her image, taken from CCTV footage, was circulated by Interpol.\nShe had already fled, first driving through Italy and Germany, then taking a bus from Frankfurt to Ukraine.\nBefore she could be caught and questioned though, she was driven to the woods by Reut and Zhykovych and killed. Each blames the other for her shooting.\nThe shocking case has prompted intense speculation, including over who may have wanted Yermolayev dead and why, and whether this could have been a state-ordered assassination attempt, a rogue operation or some kind of criminal score-settling.\nThe businessman himself, who renounced his Ukrainian passport some years ago and now has Cypriot citizenship, has dismissed multiple theories.\nThey include the idea the attack might be linked to a struggle between organised crime groups involved in highly lucrative scam call-centres in Ukraine.\nEarlier this year, a court in Estonia convicted Yermolayev's son, Artur, of defrauding its citizens out of millions of euros through such \"offisy\", as the scam networks are known in Ukraine.\nVadym Yermolayev told the Ukrainska Pravda newspaper that he \"never had anything to do with anything\" in the case.\nNow Zhykovych has put forward his own theory to us.\nHe alleges that Reut told him the bombing was in retaliation for \"funding the annexation of Crimea\", which he understood to mean Yermolayev was paying taxes to Russia from businesses in Russian-occupied Crimea.\n\"In my view, this constitutes grounds for the operation,\" he communicated from prison.\nYermolayev has repeatedly denied any remaining business interests linked to Russia.\nBut might this story be even murkier?\nAt his most recent custody hearing in Kyiv, surrounded by heavily armed guards, Zhykovych spoke publicly for the first time since his arrest. The BBC were the only media present.\nAt one point Zhykovych said Reut had in fact told him the attack in Monaco was not \"authorised\".\n\"Someone had ordered this target from the civilian side,\" Zhykovych said, without explaining.\nThe judge then interrupted, reminding him that he was addressing an open court.\nZhykovych also revealed that Reut originally talked of two targets.\nWhen we asked, he said he could not disclose the second name. Other sources strongly suggest it was a pro-Russian blogger tried and convicted in absentia last year by Ukraine of treason.\nAs the investigation continues – into both the bombing in Monaco and the murder in Ukraine - Berezovska's family have many questions of their own.\nThe 39-year-old had been in Germany since early 2022, when she left Ukraine as a refugee with her young son.\nZhykovych now claims she was living a double-life, working with him as an agent \"against Muscovy\" – meaning Russia.\nHe said they had met online and told us the pair were working to \"repel the armed aggression of the Russian Federation\".\nBerezovska's husband has told the BBC that the allegation was \"nonsense\". He believes she was dragged, unwittingly, into the whole affair.\nZhykovych says Berezovska called him the day after the Monaco attack, and when he asked why she had done it, she said Reut had promised her a huge fee. \"$50,000 doesn't just lie on the streets,\" she supposedly explained.\nResidents in her village have told us that Berezovska was saving to buy a flat. But when she travelled to Ukraine to collect the money, she was lured into the woods and shot.\nAdditional reporting by Anastasiia Levchenko and Volodymyr Lozhko.\nRelated topics\nEurope\nKyiv\nUkraine\nMonaco\nMore on this story\nWoman suspected of Monaco bomb attack found dead in Ukraine\nPublished\n7 July", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T01:27:43.086036", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "モナコ", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.537, "sm": 125, "em": 537, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "で", "s": 0.55, "e": 0.663, "sm": 550, "em": 662, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "6", "s": 0.675, "e": 0.988, "sm": 675, "em": 987, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "月", "s": 0.988, "e": 1.3, "sm": 987, "em": 1300, "cs": 5, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "、", "s": 1.3, "e": 1.538, "sm": 1300, "em": 1537, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"